Purpose: Land build-plan-08 phase 1 on road_kit_dev -- ROAD_PERMISSIONS.IS_RESERVED,
  ROAD_ROLE_PERMISSIONS.ATTACHED_AT/ATTACHED_BY, the new road.role.compose permission, and
  marking the five framework permissions reserved.
Approach: ALTER first (tolerate "already exists" so the script is re-runnable), then
  95_data.sql (seeds road.role.compose, grants it to road.system_admin, and runs the explicit
  UPDATE that marks pre-existing rows reserved -- the ALTER's DEFAULT 'N' would otherwise leave
  them fail-open until this runs), then 99_verify.sql.
Reason: build-plan-08 phase 1, backporting spec patch 07 to road-kit. road_kit_dev was fully
  deployed on 2026-08-18 and holds live rows, so this is an incremental ALTER against a
  deployed schema, not a fresh CREATE. Byte-identical in approach to road-cal's own
  scratch/phase1-composition-apply.sql, which ran SUCCESS on 2026-08-19.
Expected objects:
  ROAD_PERMISSIONS (altered: IS_RESERVED, ROAD_PERMISSIONS_RESERVED_CK)
  ROAD_ROLE_PERMISSIONS (altered: ATTACHED_AT, ATTACHED_BY, its FK to ROAD_PRINCIPALS)
  ROAD_PERMISSIONS: road.role.compose (new row, reserved)
  ROAD_ROLE_PERMISSIONS: road.system_admin -> road.role.compose
Risk: Low. Additive columns with defaults; no existing column, constraint or row is removed. The
  UPDATE only flips IS_RESERVED 'N' -> 'Y' on five named rows, which is reversible.
  Deliberately does NOT create the assertions -- that is phase 2, and phase 1 must not be
  committed without it (build-plan-08 section 2).
Prior history checked: road-cal logs/dev/runs/20260819_130422_phase1-composition-apply_963.log
  is the identical operation against road_cal_dev, SUCCESS. No prior road-kit ALTER of either
  table exists.
